WEBVTT

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.380
I'm sorry, everyone...

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:44.620
It's all because I'm filthy.

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:47.300
I'm so sorry...

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:51.400
Episode 5: "Asahi Haruka"

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:51.400
The cursed girl, Asahi Haruka?

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:52.400
Yeah.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:55.650
We got a letter in the Monster Mailbox
Shizuru set up.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:56.660
<b>Mail</b>

00:00:56.660 --> 00:01:00.660
Um... "Are you all familiar with 
the story of Asahi Haruka?

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:05.410
If you attempt to investigate her
and disturb her slumber,

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:07.540
you will be placed under her curse.

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:11.640
In a certain forest, there is an orphanage.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:16.670
After a girl called 
Asahi Haruka arrived there,

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:19.140
strange things began to occur.

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:22.560
Windows and mirrors would 
shatter on their own,

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:25.210
and the pets would suddenly pass away...

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:28.970
Before long, it affected the 
children and teachers, too...

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:33.530
In the end, the orphanage was closed down."

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:38.550
I feel like I've heard this story before.

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:40.580
"Seven years ago,

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:44.170
a boy from that orphanage transferred into
the school I was attending at the time,

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:47.760
Kazamatsuri 7th Municipal Elementary School.

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:51.710
A few days after he told us 
the story of Asahi Haruka,

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:55.240
he died of a strange, unknown illness.

00:01:55.910 --> 00:01:59.140
He was cursed for disturbing her slumber.

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:03.220
His name was Kishida Ryuugo, 
and he was in Class 4-1."

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:05.700
Things got awfully specific all of a sudden.

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:06.430
Right?

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:08.480
If he was in 4th grade seven years ago,

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:10.400
then he would've been the same age as us.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.890
I'm pretty sure Yoshino is 
from 7th Elementary, too.

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:14.780
Corroborating this story should be easy,

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:16.570
and then I'll get to
touch the president's boo—

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:20.950
By the way, where are 
Shizuru and the class rep?

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:25.620
Maybe they're finding it hard to come,

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:27.330
considering what happened yesterday.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.710
Are you still fighting?

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:32.210
It's not like we fought or anything...

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:34.210
Good grief.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:35.540
Before investigating,

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:38.180
we've first gotta fix things
between Chihaya and the class rep.

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:42.680
Why Lucia wears gloves?

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:43.640
Yeah.

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:47.030
Sure, she may be a hypochondriac,
but it seems a little excessive.

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:51.080
And given what happened yesterday,
I figured I should at least ask why.

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:54.890
Kotarou...

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:57.940
Are you Lucia's friend?

00:02:58.500 --> 00:02:59.700
Yeah. Or at least I think so.

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:04.700
Then I don't mind telling you Lucia's secret.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:06.320
Secret?

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:11.200
So long as you will be
Lucia's friend forever...

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:19.400
The class rep's secret, huh?

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:26.470
What is it? I'm busy right now.

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:28.070
<i>Oh, out on a date?</i>

00:03:28.070 --> 00:03:29.280
I'll kill you.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:32.440
<i>By the way, you went to 
7th Elementary, right?</i>

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:34.230
<i>In 4th grade, which class were you in?</i>

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:36.480
Why do you ask?

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:41.280
Sorry, but I'm not playing along.

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:44.310
I'm not a fan of disturbing the dead.

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:47.060
<i>Does that mean a transfer 
student named Kishida</i>

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:49.120
<i>really did die due to some 
strange, unknown illness?</i>

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:50.350
<i>Like I'd know!</i>

00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:52.370
<i>And I wouldn't tell you even if I did.</i>

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:56.350
<i>I may have never spoken to him,
but he was still my friend.</i>

00:03:56.740 --> 00:03:57.630
I see.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:03:58.700
Sorry about this.

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:01.110
<i>Wait. Why are you sticking 
your nose into all this?</i>

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:03.590
Something about it just stuck out in my mind.

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:05.760
I feel like I can't ignore this case.

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:07.370
Tennouji.

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:09.840
I'll give you one warning.

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:12.290
If things start looking dicey, back off.

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:13.270
<i>What do you mean, dicey?</i>

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:15.790
If the glass shatters, watch your back.

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:16.640
<i>Glass?</i>

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:17.520
<i>What do you mean?</i>

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:19.150
I'm done talking about this.

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:31.960
This is all the help I can give you.

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:34.590
Get by on your own luck from here on out.

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:38.520
That roster is a part of my history.

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:40.960
Give it back as soon as you're done with it.

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:45.190
Thank you, Yoshino.

00:04:45.190 --> 00:04:47.970
Could you make copies of this
for the whole class?

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:48.770
Yes.

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:51.470
I'll lend you my copy card.

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:53.230
<b>Please use as little 
copier paper as possible.
Let's use recycled paper.
-Vice Principal</b>

00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:57.580
Class Rep!

00:04:57.580 --> 00:04:58.970
What, Tennouji?

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:01.240
Hey! This isn't for personal use!

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:02.260
It's just one copy.

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:03.240
Overlook this for me.

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:04.560
Jeez...

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:07.490
What are you copying?

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:09.630
Sorry, but it's a secret.

00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:12.370
If you knew, you could be cursed.

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:14.370
Did you say "cursed"?

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:16.840
Thanks, Class Rep!

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:18.710
Honestly...

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:25.230
I guess I should give everyone a call.

00:05:25.230 --> 00:05:26.380
Wait, Tennouji!

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:29.500
You left this in the tray.

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:30.640
It's yours, right?

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:31.640
Do not wake me.

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:32.640
Or else, you will

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:37.930
What is this?

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:39.650
I don't remember copying anything like—

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:46.230
If the glass shatters, watch your back.

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:48.780
It couldn't be, right?

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:50.600
It couldn't be what?

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:51.950
Oh, nothing...

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:54.250
What are you plotting this time?

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:57.710
Depending on your answer,
Tennouji Kotarou, I might have to...

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:04.890
So you're telling me that note 
is a warning from Asahi Haruka,

00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:07.090
and that she shattered the glass?

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:07.720
Do not wake me.

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:07.720
Or else, you will...

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:08.220
No.

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:12.000
The copier must've spat out the wrong sheet.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.600
But that note...

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:15.100
Probably just used paper.

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:17.930
Maybe a recycled sheet got mixed in?

00:06:17.930 --> 00:06:19.020
But...

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:22.610
As for the windows, someone must 
have thrown a rock or something.

00:06:22.870 --> 00:06:24.980
You don't believe in curses?

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:29.360
Well, you could say I have a reason 
for not wanting to in this case.

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:32.730
Anyway, I want to prove there's 
no such thing as curses

00:06:32.730 --> 00:06:34.870
and clear that girl's name.

00:06:35.420 --> 00:06:36.620
Clear her name?

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:41.100
If all of this is hurting 
Asahi Haruka to this day,

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:43.380
the occult club just can't leave it as-is.

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:46.630
You have a point...

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:48.440
Then it's settled.

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:52.390
Let's shut down this cheap horror story!

00:06:53.690 --> 00:06:55.390
Y-Yeah.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:04.170
Shut it down, huh?

00:07:05.450 --> 00:07:08.450
Oh, yeah. The forecast did call for rain.

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:15.080
Why do you wake me?

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:15.910
Huh?

00:07:17.390 --> 00:07:20.080
Why do you wake me?

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:27.350
We are both burdened by 
the same sorrow, too...

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:32.150
Do not wake me...

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:34.080
Or else...

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:36.180
You will...

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:45.610
No!

00:07:47.220 --> 00:07:48.680
<i>Th-The glass!</i>

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:50.610
Um, are you okay?

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:52.210
<i>That's why I said no!</i>

00:07:52.210 --> 00:07:53.680
<i>This is the same as four years ago!</i>

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:56.100
<i>The curse hasn't gone away!</i>

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:57.340
Uh, hang on!

00:07:58.650 --> 00:08:00.030
Seriously?

00:08:00.590 --> 00:08:03.540
<i>Strangely, every person I called
got really scared</i>

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:05.130
<i>the second I brought up Asahi Haruka</i>

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:08.090
<i>and refused to answer any questions.</i>

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:10.430
<i>In addition, after my call,</i>

00:08:10.430 --> 00:08:14.010
<i>they all mysteriously experienced
their windows or mirrors breaking...</i>

00:08:14.740 --> 00:08:17.760
I left contacting the girls 
up to the class rep...

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:20.080
All right, one more person!

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:25.470
Oh, is this Wada Kenji-kun's residence?

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:26.490
Sorry to call so late—

00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:29.100
Huh? He isn't there?

00:08:37.480 --> 00:08:38.960
That's for the best.

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:44.870
Remember our suffering...

00:08:45.730 --> 00:08:48.000
N-No.

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:51.500
I decided to face it!

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:53.010
That is impossible.

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:56.530
After all, we really are...

00:08:57.120 --> 00:08:59.450
...cursed.

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:09.020
I wonder if the class rep is absent?

00:09:10.770 --> 00:09:14.780
I thought I would get to apologize 
to her today for sure...

00:09:17.780 --> 00:09:18.780
Class Rep

00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:21.820
It's not like her to be absent without leave.

00:09:21.820 --> 00:09:23.790
Hi, Tennouji-kun.

00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:25.040
Inoue.

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:28.550
I hear you're after a dangerous scoop?

00:09:28.550 --> 00:09:29.900
How do you know that?

00:09:30.850 --> 00:09:35.620
That story is frankly considered off-limits
 among us reporters.

00:09:35.620 --> 00:09:36.050
Huh?

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:42.560
<b>Kazamatsuri 
Middle School</b>

00:09:36.410 --> 00:09:39.140
Someone who was researching it
got into an accident.

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:42.560
This has a column written by him.

00:09:42.920 --> 00:09:43.930
Accidents?

00:09:44.210 --> 00:09:47.630
If you're my rival,
pursuing the mysteries of Kazamatsuri,

00:09:47.630 --> 00:09:49.480
then handle the rest on your own.

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:51.940
Just to let you know, you owe me one.

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:51.940
Hey!

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:56.450
<b>Baraki Kunihiko's Column
"The Borderline Between Ghost 
Stories and Urban Legends"</b>

00:09:57.060 --> 00:09:58.120
Baraki?

00:10:01.810 --> 00:10:05.390
This is a recording from
7th Elementary Class 4-1's reunion.

00:10:05.770 --> 00:10:08.710
All of the glass in the entire venue
shattered out of nowhere.

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:10.760
And, on the way back from the event,

00:10:10.760 --> 00:10:13.240
a huge billboard fell right in front of me.

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:16.480
If it had actually hit me,
I'd be dead for sure.

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:18.160
I hear the rumors embellished it

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:20.970
and say I got seriously hurt, though!

00:10:22.630 --> 00:10:24.720
In the end, all I was able to
get out of anyone

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:26.560
was that late Kishida Ryuugo lived in

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:29.940
an orphanage called
"The Santa Brosia Peace Garden."

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:38.260
Do not wake me.

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:50.710
I-It can't be.

00:10:57.850 --> 00:10:59.720
Class Rep?

00:11:00.020 --> 00:11:02.900
Do not wake me.

00:11:03.340 --> 00:11:06.270
This is your final warning.

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:07.890
Class Rep!

00:11:11.430 --> 00:11:12.380
Hey!

00:11:13.130 --> 00:11:14.310
Damn!

00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:19.620
Hang in there.

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:21.350
I'm here for you.

00:11:21.350 --> 00:11:23.180
No, Sensei...

00:11:23.570 --> 00:11:25.330
If you touch me...

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:27.130
What's wrong?

00:11:32.190 --> 00:11:33.940
It was a dream?

00:11:35.800 --> 00:11:37.000
Are you okay?

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:38.720
Thank goodness.

00:11:38.720 --> 00:11:39.920
You came to?

00:11:40.400 --> 00:11:42.250
Tennouji?

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:44.420
I see.

00:11:44.420 --> 00:11:45.640
That's what happened?

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:48.120
Uh, about how you're dressed, um...

00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:49.750
I thought you would catch a cold.

00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:53.650
I-I didn't look, a-and I didn't 
touch your skin or anything, either.

00:11:54.100 --> 00:11:55.300
I see.

00:11:55.300 --> 00:11:56.650
That's good.

00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:05.410
Watch.

00:12:09.530 --> 00:12:11.160
Wh-What just happened?

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:13.850
It's the curse of Asahi Haruka.

00:12:13.850 --> 00:12:15.900
When I touch plants, they wither.

00:12:17.190 --> 00:12:18.300
Don't tell me...

00:12:19.260 --> 00:12:20.850
Is this my fault?

00:12:20.850 --> 00:12:22.880
Were you cursed in retribution

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:25.050
for me not giving up on my investigation?

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:27.390
Don't worry about it, Tennouji.

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:30.310
Even if that were the case,

00:12:30.820 --> 00:12:32.430
it would change nothing for me.

00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:38.940
Lucia experienced an unfortunate 
incident when she was young.

00:12:39.310 --> 00:12:42.150
She made the plants and 
animals raised in her class

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:45.450
wither and die one after another.

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:47.980
Surely it was just a coincidence?

00:12:47.980 --> 00:12:52.740
Lucia convinced herself 
that it was her fault, though.

00:12:53.220 --> 00:12:55.770
She thought it was because 
her hands were filthy...

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:02.210
That's why Lucia is too afraid to 
touch any living thing to this day.

00:13:02.660 --> 00:13:06.370
Lucia has faced that trauma 
head-on in her own way.

00:13:06.370 --> 00:13:08.600
She's attempted to overcome it.

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:13.320
And her gloves provide her the most respite.

00:13:14.370 --> 00:13:18.360
I could just wear my gloves forever
and never touch anyone.

00:13:18.700 --> 00:13:20.160
Nothing will change.

00:13:20.670 --> 00:13:21.630
Nothing.

00:13:22.150 --> 00:13:23.110
Nothing!

00:13:23.710 --> 00:13:25.820
So it won't be painful...

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:27.870
I'm filthy.

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:29.080
I'm unclean, so—

00:13:29.080 --> 00:13:31.370
No! You're wrong about that!

00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:35.590
You don't understand!

00:13:35.590 --> 00:13:38.380
Not my sorrow,
nor Asahi Haruka's suffering!

00:13:40.850 --> 00:13:42.320
I always knew.

00:13:43.020 --> 00:13:46.840
There's no world that can accept 
people as filthy as we are.

00:13:47.530 --> 00:13:48.390
I...

00:13:49.150 --> 00:13:51.160
We will live the rest of our lives

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:55.020
all alone, never touching another person.

00:13:55.670 --> 00:13:58.760
That's how it has to be!

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:01.660
<i>Why did it turn out this way?</i>

00:14:02.600 --> 00:14:04.280
<i>I just...</i>

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:07.780
Santa Brosia Peace Garden

00:14:09.280 --> 00:14:11.280
<b>No Trespassing</b>

00:14:09.280 --> 00:14:11.280
Class Four Industrial Toxic 
Waste Treatment Plant

00:14:09.280 --> 00:14:11.280
Entering this site without permission is forbidden.

00:14:11.640 --> 00:14:14.560
This is the entrance to the orphanage?

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:17.660
Well, I guess I've got no choice
but to check it out.

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:31.760
<i>It </i>does<i> look like children were here.</i>

00:14:47.970 --> 00:14:49.940
This is Kishida Ryuugo?

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:51.860
Asahi Haruka is...

00:14:55.520 --> 00:14:58.320
Found you, Asahi Haruka.

00:14:58.750 --> 00:14:59.540
No...

00:15:01.180 --> 00:15:02.700
Konohana Lucia!

00:15:04.070 --> 00:15:06.050
How did you know it was me?

00:15:06.450 --> 00:15:07.660
This.

00:15:07.660 --> 00:15:08.420
The roster?

00:15:08.650 --> 00:15:09.580
Yeah.

00:15:09.580 --> 00:15:13.380
The Wada Kenji on this list doesn't 
live at this address anymore.

00:15:13.380 --> 00:15:14.490
He moved.

00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:17.500
And yet, the glass in that 
house shattered, too.

00:15:17.880 --> 00:15:20.090
A curse wouldn't make that mistake, would it?

00:15:20.780 --> 00:15:23.900
The only ones with this roster
 are Yoshino, myself,

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:25.940
and you, Class Rep.

00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:27.470
I see.

00:15:27.470 --> 00:15:29.500
I made a pretty lame mistake.

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:34.950
When I made that copy, you looked 
at the data left on the copier

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:37.950
and figured out what I was 
trying to investigate, right?

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:41.610
That said, I couldn't figure out
how you shattered all that glass.

00:15:45.430 --> 00:15:46.390
You're right.

00:15:46.390 --> 00:15:49.320
By forging that warning
and shattering the glass,

00:15:49.320 --> 00:15:51.720
I tried to get you to stop your investigation,

00:15:52.310 --> 00:15:54.370
but you wouldn't give up.

00:15:54.370 --> 00:15:55.220
Class Rep.

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:56.960
No, Lucia.

00:15:56.960 --> 00:15:58.060
Why are you doing this?

00:15:58.060 --> 00:16:01.470
I can't touch anything alive.

00:16:01.850 --> 00:16:06.990
I was born normal, but was reborn 
this way at a certain place.

00:16:07.380 --> 00:16:09.110
"This way"?

00:16:09.500 --> 00:16:12.090
You'll never understand if 
I simply tell you about it.

00:16:12.090 --> 00:16:15.520
But this hand's curse is real.

00:16:15.860 --> 00:16:18.870
I can shatter glass without 
laying a finger on it, too.

00:16:21.170 --> 00:16:23.160
The poison that dwells in these hands

00:16:23.160 --> 00:16:26.500
can take the life of anything 
they touch, not just plants.

00:16:27.590 --> 00:16:29.380
I didn't want anyone to know

00:16:29.970 --> 00:16:32.420
about my hideous past, or my true identity.

00:16:33.310 --> 00:16:34.580
I see.

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:37.350
That's the curse's true form?

00:16:37.690 --> 00:16:41.490
This area is still heavily laced
with my poison.

00:16:41.840 --> 00:16:43.330
I'm saying this for your own good.

00:16:43.330 --> 00:16:45.400
Leave here immediately and seek treatment.

00:16:45.740 --> 00:16:47.110
You can still make it in time.

00:16:49.340 --> 00:16:50.440
Tennouji?!

00:16:51.640 --> 00:16:52.440
Hey!

00:16:57.600 --> 00:16:59.690
Don't tell me, back then...

00:16:59.690 --> 00:17:01.640
H-Hurry to the hospital!

00:17:01.640 --> 00:17:02.420
No...

00:17:02.420 --> 00:17:04.210
The hospital can't help anymore...

00:17:04.210 --> 00:17:06.140
I'm sorry, Tennouji.

00:17:06.140 --> 00:17:08.120
What have I done?

00:17:08.120 --> 00:17:10.400
No, I'm the one who should apologize.

00:17:10.400 --> 00:17:10.920
Huh?

00:17:11.300 --> 00:17:12.310
I'm sorry.

00:17:12.660 --> 00:17:17.440
If only I'd been strong enough to
withstand your poison back then,

00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:23.180
I could have prevented you
from suffering again.

00:17:23.470 --> 00:17:25.040
That's not your fault—

00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:26.200
No!

00:17:26.550 --> 00:17:30.410
To be honest, I've got 
an unusual power myself.

00:17:31.020 --> 00:17:32.070
A power?

00:17:37.520 --> 00:17:40.160
Wh-What are you doing, Tennouji?

00:17:40.600 --> 00:17:43.040
<i>I have to rewrite my body.</i>

00:17:43.640 --> 00:17:45.660
<i>Rewrite it into one that 
can withstand the poison.</i>

00:18:07.570 --> 00:18:08.940
Ow...

00:18:11.140 --> 00:18:14.570
I've accepted Konohana Lucia's world!

00:18:14.900 --> 00:18:16.900
How?

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:19.930
This is my power.
That's the only way I can explain it.

00:18:20.760 --> 00:18:22.860
What are you?

00:18:23.300 --> 00:18:24.160
Don't tell me...

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:29.280
I'm Tennouji Kotarou, 
Konohana Lucia's friend!

00:18:29.280 --> 00:18:31.270
My friend?

00:18:31.270 --> 00:18:32.990
Yeah, so...

00:18:34.080 --> 00:18:38.760
So never again say you'll spend your life
all alone, never touching anyone...

00:18:39.250 --> 00:18:41.050
It's just too sad.

00:18:41.860 --> 00:18:44.580
Tennouji...

00:18:45.220 --> 00:18:48.680
And besides, you're not alone at all.

00:18:50.580 --> 00:18:53.090
You have Shizuru, and you have me.

00:18:53.090 --> 00:18:54.960
And everyone at the occult club, too.

00:18:54.960 --> 00:18:57.190
Chihaya and Kotori were worried about you!

00:18:57.190 --> 00:18:58.820
And, well, probably the president, too.

00:19:00.140 --> 00:19:03.830
You know, friends don't let
 friends be all alone.

00:19:08.670 --> 00:19:09.840
Impossible.

00:19:10.480 --> 00:19:11.460
It's a miracle...

00:19:12.120 --> 00:19:16.210
What's wrong with a miracle or two?

00:19:16.940 --> 00:19:19.720
After all, this is a chapel, isn't it?

00:19:23.100 --> 00:19:23.870
Yeah.

00:19:25.840 --> 00:19:26.480
Yeah!

00:19:37.990 --> 00:19:40.500
Oh, are we interrupting?

00:19:40.940 --> 00:19:42.740
Wh-Who are you people?

00:19:43.020 --> 00:19:44.500
I-It's all right.

00:19:44.800 --> 00:19:47.740
They're, um... my allies.

00:19:48.320 --> 00:19:49.250
Allies?

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:54.800
Hi!

00:19:56.210 --> 00:19:57.500
That was a surprise.

00:19:57.840 --> 00:20:01.760
It's hard to believe you're resistant 
to Lucia-chan's poison by nature.

00:20:01.990 --> 00:20:02.890
Forget about that.

00:20:02.890 --> 00:20:05.530
Who are you and the others?

00:20:05.530 --> 00:20:07.510
You avoided the question the other day,

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:11.520
but does Lucia have something to do 
with Shizuru's organization, too?

00:20:11.960 --> 00:20:13.900
You know about Shizuru, too?

00:20:14.550 --> 00:20:15.860
Guardian.

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:18.020
That is our organization.

00:20:18.350 --> 00:20:20.910
Nishikujou-san! You can't mention that name!

00:20:20.910 --> 00:20:23.340
It's better than having him snoop around.

00:20:23.340 --> 00:20:25.810
This incident made that clear, didn't it?

00:20:25.810 --> 00:20:27.030
Well...

00:20:27.460 --> 00:20:33.190
Our organization is gathering people with
special powers for a certain purpose.

00:20:33.520 --> 00:20:37.290
Lucia-chan and Shizuru-chan 
possess those special powers.

00:20:37.750 --> 00:20:39.310
Special powers?

00:20:40.220 --> 00:20:43.550
So what in the world is 
this organization trying to do?

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:46.550
We're protecting the Earth.

00:20:46.870 --> 00:20:48.680
Protecting the Earth?

00:20:48.990 --> 00:20:53.340
Right now, Kazamatsuri City 
is in a volatile situation

00:20:53.340 --> 00:20:57.800
due to an individual who holds the key
to Earth's survival or its destruction.

00:20:57.800 --> 00:20:59.960
That doesn't sound very nice.

00:20:59.960 --> 00:21:01.370
You believe us?

00:21:01.370 --> 00:21:04.510
All this nonsense about how
Earth could be destroyed?

00:21:04.510 --> 00:21:08.070
I doubt you'd lie in this situation.

00:21:08.360 --> 00:21:11.580
We call that person the Key.

00:21:12.010 --> 00:21:12.950
The Key?

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:14.720
The Key's existence

00:21:14.720 --> 00:21:19.000
could have a profound effect on
 the world and all of its faiths.

00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:22.130
As such, we cannot even
make their existence public.

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:24.820
To make matters worse, there are 
those who would shelter the Key

00:21:24.820 --> 00:21:27.800
and advocate that Earth <i>should</i> perish.

00:21:27.800 --> 00:21:29.030
What the heck?

00:21:29.030 --> 00:21:30.560
Are they a cult?

00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:34.980
It's an organization we currently
consider to be the most dangerous,

00:21:34.980 --> 00:21:36.810
and it's called Gaia.

00:21:37.080 --> 00:21:38.200
Gaia?

00:21:38.200 --> 00:21:41.120
It's a fanatical organization
that believes the Key

00:21:41.120 --> 00:21:42.680
will bring about Earth's regeneration.

00:21:43.870 --> 00:21:47.760
I'm sorry, but that's all 
we can tell you right now.

00:21:47.760 --> 00:21:51.980
Now you have no choice but 
to keep this secret.

00:21:51.980 --> 00:21:54.330
Will you keep quiet about this?

00:21:55.160 --> 00:21:56.330
Or will you...

00:21:56.590 --> 00:21:59.540
In that case, I have a condition of my own.

00:21:59.540 --> 00:22:00.840
Oh, what is it?

00:22:02.880 --> 00:22:05.090
I want to eat a lunch made by Lucia!

00:22:06.230 --> 00:22:07.340
What?!

00:22:09.680 --> 00:22:11.350
Why me?!

00:22:11.540 --> 00:22:13.780
By the way, you must wear
a maid's uniform at the same time!

00:22:13.780 --> 00:22:14.850
This is non-negotiable!

00:22:14.850 --> 00:22:17.720
D-Damn you! Who would wear 
something like that?!

00:22:17.720 --> 00:22:19.160
Oh, and also, call me Master—

00:22:19.160 --> 00:22:21.310
Don't get carried away!
